{{Card Infobox|Cost=3|Rarity=Common|Type=Troop|Arena=Jungle Arena|ReleaseDate=24 February 2017}}
{{Quote|Spawns Six Goblins - three with knives, three with spears - at a discounted Elixir cost. It's like a Goblin Value Pack!}}

The Goblin Gang is a {{Rarity|Common}} [[Cards|card]] that is unlocked from the [[Arenas|Jungle Arena (Arena 9)]]. It spawns three [[Goblins]] and three [[Spear Goblins]] in a hexagon formation. The Goblins will spawn before the Spear Goblins. A Goblin Gang card costs 3 [[Elixir]] to deploy.

==Strategy==
{{Battle Deck with Card|:Category:Battle Decks using the Goblin Gang Card}}
*Even though the Goblin Gang spawns both [[Goblins]] and [[Spear Goblins]] at once, using both of these [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] as two [[cards]] in the same [[Battle Decks|deck]] has the advantage of being able to be deployed separately, such that they cannot be countered all at once by splash damage troops such as the [[Valkyrie]], [[Dark Prince]], [[Royal Ghost]], and the Mega Knight.
*Because of their placement, the Goblins in front, which have more health, will tank for the Spear Goblins behind, creating a mini-push, though the Goblins actually deal much more damage than the Spear Goblins.
*It can be risky to deploy the Goblin Gang on one lane since [[The Log]] can completely counter the Goblin Gang for a positive [[Elixir]] trade. However, they can be used to bait the opponent's [[Arrows]] or The Log.
*An [[Electro Wizard]] or a Valkyrie spawned on top of the Goblin Gang can make short work of this card and will be able to set up for a counter push.
*This card can provide a decent distraction for enemy high damage single-targeting troops like the [[P.E.K.K.A.|P.E.K.K.A]], [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.|Mini P.E.K.K.A]], [[Inferno Dragon]], [[Mighty Miner]], or the [[Prince]], giving time for you to finish these troops off.
*An unsupported P.E.K.K.A. can be defeated by a Goblin Gang in the right placement with the assistance of a [[:Category:Tower Troop Cards|Crown Tower]].
*The Goblin Gang can be used to surround and destroy non-360 degree splash units (excluding the [[Bomber]] and [[Wizard]] due to their large splash range) as they will not be able to kill all of the spawned Goblins and Spear Goblins at once.
*An [[Ice Spirit]] or [[Electro Spirit]] can tank one or two hits and then freeze/stun a Crown Tower, potentially allowing the Goblin Gang to deal massive damage.
*Using a [[Mirror]] and a [[Clone]] together on this card is a very risky strategy unless the player is certain the opponent has no splash damage, but it has the potential to swarm or rush the enemy.
*A high Level Goblin Gang's Goblins will take three shots instead of two from the Crown Tower, allowing it to deal much more damage than if it was at equivalent Level. Keep this in mind whenever rushing a lane with a Goblin Gang.
*The Goblin Gang can completely shut down a [[Goblin Barrel]] if timed properly.
*When countering [[Elite Barbarians]], placing the Goblin Gang with the corner most Goblin nearest to both Elite Barbarians will make them both attack one Goblin the entire time, increasing the time the Goblin Gang can stall them. This way, (assuming both cards are a similar level) only one heavily damaged Elite Barbarian will make it to the Tower.
*The Goblin Gang can completely shut down a [[Hog Rider]] when timed correctly and placed in front of him.
*When distracting a [[Mortar]], placing the Goblin Gang in the centre will effectively optimize the amount of time the Mortar stays distracted, giving you more time to finish it off.
*When defending against a lone [[Golem]], take advantage of the range that the Spear Goblins have. Placing the Goblin Gang at a distance will prevent the Spear Goblins from being killed by the Golem's Death Damage so that the Spear Goblins defend against the spawned Golemites, preventing more damage from being dealt to the Tower.
*The Goblin Gang can be used to defend against fragile air units like the [[Flying Machine]], [[Bats]], and [[Minion Horde]]. The Goblins will tank the damage from the air units, while the Spear Goblins will attack the air units. This is especially key when defending against the [[Baby Dragon]] or the [[Electro Dragon]], as their damage is not enough to one-shot the Goblins.
*The Goblin Gang can completely stop a lone [[Mega Knight]] if placed correctly.
*Skeleton Army can be used as an alternative to the Goblin Gang. However, it has much less hitpoints per unit, making it weak to more [[:Category:Spell Cards|spells]], the Skeletons also move slower, making it less threatening in offense, and cannot hit air troops. In exchange, the Skeleton Army has more total damage than Goblin Gang and comes with more units overall.

